From f51c577542a53e6684b79348334be1cf4ea1efe6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:44:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): cached sessions as offline-marked rows in the
 normal sidebar; drop standalone hub-sync section [daveey]

* fix(desktop): cached offline sessions join the normal sidebar list instead of a standalone history section [daveey]

hub-sync no longer contributes a "Synced from other gateways" section. Replica session
rows of unreachable gateways become fallback inputs to the ordinary sidebar list (SessionInfo
with offline_cached markers), so the automated/test toggle, hidden gateways, profile scope,
pins, grouping and ordering apply to them. Eligibility reuses SIDEBAR_EXCLUDED_SOURCES; live
rows win on identity and a live connection drops its cached rows; is_active is never claimed;
last_active is the session activity, not the sync time. Opening a cached row says the gateway
is offline; archive/rename queue as hub owner requests.

* fix(desktop): keep code-health caps for cached-session sidebar (extract hook, row mark, archive helper) [daveey]

---------

Co-authored-by: David Bloomin <452472+daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
